    <text>
        <body>
            <div>
                <head>Translated parts</head>
                <p xml:id="KR1e0008-start">
                    <seg corresp="#KR1e0008_tls_011-7a.2" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T08:05:10.249+09:00">Ninth month.</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#KR1e0008_tls_011-7a.3" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T08:05:16.382+09:00">Great Rain Sacrifice.</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#KR1e0008_tls_011-7a.4" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T08:05:41.985+09:00">When a Rain Sacrifice record is dated to the month,</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#KR1e0008_tls_011-7a.5" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T08:05:48.116+09:00">it indicates the appropriateness of the Rain Sacrifice.</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#KR1e0008_tls_011-7a.6" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T08:06:25.815+09:00">A record of the form “Autumn. Great Rain Sacrifice”</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#KR1e0008_tls_011-7a.7" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T08:06:41.687+09:00">is not proper</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#KR1e0008_tls_011-7a.8" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T08:06:52.535+09:00">and a record of the form “Winter. Great Rain Sacrifice”</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#KR1e0008_tls_011-7a.9" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T08:07:07.489+09:00">is not proper.</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#KR1e0008_tls_011-7a.10" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T08:07:32.881+09:00">What is it about the record “Autumn. Great Rain Sacrifice” that indicates that the Rain Sacrifice should be considered improper?</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#KR1e0008_tls_011-7a.11" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T08:07:54.276+09:00">Before the moisture in the vegetation has been fully depleted</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#KR1e0008_tls_011-7a.12" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T08:08:04.597+09:00">and human effort has been fully spent,</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#KR1e0008_tls_011-7a.13" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T08:08:23.547+09:00">it is not yet permissible to perform the Great Rain Sacrifice.</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#KR1e0008_tls_011-7a.14" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T08:08:43.236+09:00">Given that “a Rain Sacrifice record dated to the month</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#KR1e0008_tls_011-7a.15" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T08:08:55.605+09:00">indicates the appropriateness of the Rain Sacrifice”,</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#KR1e0008_tls_011-7a.16" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T08:09:08.764+09:00">why does the month indicate that the Rain Sacrifice was proper?</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#KR1e0008_tls_011-7a.17" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T08:10:01.092+09:00">The appropriateness of the Rain Sacrifice is only achieved when the Rain Sacrifice is performed after the appropriate time of waiting has come to its end</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#KR1e0008_tls_011-7a.18" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T08:14:55.475+09:00">and all human efforts have been exhausted.</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#KR1e0008_tls_011-7a.21" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T08:18:34.212+09:00">What is the meaning of “the appropriate time of waiting has come to its end</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#KR1e0008_tls_011-7a.22" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T08:18:48.158+09:00">and all human efforts have been exhausted”?</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#KR1e0008_tls_011-7a.23" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T08:18:58.862+09:00">If in this very month it does not rain,</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#KR1e0008_tls_011-7a.24" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T08:19:12.49+09:00">there will be no crop maturation;</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#KR1e0008_tls_011-7a.25" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T08:19:24.737+09:00">and if in this very year we do not reap the harvest,</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#KR1e0008_tls_011-7a.26" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T08:19:40.347+09:00">there will be no food.</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#KR1e0008_tls_011-7a.27" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T08:19:50.846+09:00">This is the meaning of “the proper time of waiting has come to its end</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#KR1e0008_tls_011-7a.28" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T08:20:11.159+09:00">and all human efforts have been exhausted”.</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#KR1e0008_tls_011-7a.29" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T08:20:23.654+09:00">Why must the Rain Sacrifice wait until “the appropriate time of waiting has come to its end</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#KR1e0008_tls_011-7a.30" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T08:20:32.465+09:00">and all human efforts have been exhausted”?</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#KR1e0008_tls_011-7a.31" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T08:20:42.801+09:00">The Rain Sacrifice is a request on account of a drought.</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#KR1e0008_tls_011-7a.33" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T08:20:50.678+09:00">To request is to supplicate.</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#KR1e0008_tls_011-7a.34" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T08:20:56.417+09:00">The ancients looked upon supplication as a grave matter.</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#KR1e0008_tls_011-7a.35" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T08:21:15.665+09:00">Why was supplication looked upon as a grave matter?</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#KR1e0008_tls_011-7a.36" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T08:21:38.99+09:00">That which makes human beings human</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#KR1e0008_tls_011-7a.38" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T08:21:52.911+09:00">The principle of supplication disregards yielding</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#KR1e0008_tls_011-7a.37" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T08:21:46.148+09:00">is yielding.</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#KR1e0008_tls_011-7a.39" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T08:22:02.991+09:00">and thus abandons that which makes human beings human.</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#KR1e0008_tls_011-7a.40" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T08:22:14.448+09:00">This is the reason why the ancients considered it a grave matter. </seg>
                    <seg corresp="#KR1e0008_tls_011-7a.41" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T08:22:23.036+09:00">To whom did one offer supplication?</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#KR1e0008_tls_011-7a.42" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T08:22:48.133+09:00">One offered supplication for a response from the Lords on High.</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#KR1e0008_tls_011-7a.43" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T08:23:03.47+09:00">Among the numinous men of ancient times, there were those who resonated with the Lords on High,</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#KR1e0008_tls_011-7a.44" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T08:23:15.217+09:00">with a full understanding of the workings of Yin and Yang.</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#KR1e0008_tls_011-7a.45" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T08:23:27.349+09:00">Such rulers personally led his great officers, guided them, and with them offered supplication to the Lords on High.</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#KR1e0008_tls_011-7a.46" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T08:23:40.358+09:00">This supplication</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#KR1e0008_tls_011-7a.47" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T08:23:53.428+09:00">was not something that could be delegated to anyone else to carry out.</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#KR1e0008_tls_011-7a.48" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T08:24:24.087+09:00">It had to be done by the ruler himself.</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#KR1e0008_tls_011-7a.49" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T08:24:29.71+09:00">This is the reason why the ancients considered it a grave matter.</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#KR1e0008_tls_011-12a.4" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T08:29:28.09+09:00">Why does the record not say “The Pheasant Gate caught fire disastrously, followed by the Twin Towers”? </seg>
                    <seg corresp="#KR1e0008_tls_011-12a.6" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T08:29:41.221+09:00">To indicate that the disastrous fire started at the Twin Towers </seg>
                    <seg corresp="#KR1e0008_tls_011-12a.7" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T08:29:54.331+09:00">and avoid listing the more honorable “Pheasant Gate” next to the “disastrous fire” in the record. </seg>
                    <seg corresp="#KR1e0008_tls_011-12a.8" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T08:30:05.387+09:00">That the record first mentions the Pheasant Gate </seg>
                    <seg corresp="#KR1e0008_tls_011-12a.9" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T08:30:11.387+09:00">is to honor the honorable. </seg>
                    <seg corresp="#KR1e0008_tls_011-12a.2" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T08:30:47.78+09:00">Summer, fifth month, renchen (day 29). </seg>
                    <seg corresp="#KR1e0008_tls_011-12a.3" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T08:30:57.916+09:00">The Pheasant Gate followed by the Twin Towers caught fire disastrously. </seg>
                    <seg corresp="#KR1e0008_tls_011-14a.2" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T08:34:45.009+09:00">Winter, tenth month. </seg>
                    <seg corresp="#KR1e0008_tls_011-14a.3" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T08:35:00.705+09:00">The Pheasant Gate followed by the Twin Towers were built anew.</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#KR1e0008_tls_011-14a.4" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T08:36:01.431+09:00">To speak of something “new” </seg>
                    <seg corresp="#KR1e0008_tls_011-14a.5" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T08:36:17.407+09:00">indicates there had been something old.</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#KR1e0008_tls_011-14a.6" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T08:36:29.802+09:00">“To build” means to remake</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#KR1e0008_tls_011-14a.7" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T08:36:41.656+09:00">and also to increase the original size. </seg>
                    <seg corresp="#KR1e0008_tls_011-14a.8" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T08:36:54.783+09:00">This was improper,</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#KR1e0008_tls_011-14a.9" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T08:37:04.489+09:00">so why does the record place the honorable “Pheasant Gate” next to the expression “built anew”?</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#KR1e0008_tls_011-14a.11" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T08:37:26.424+09:00">Though the renewal was improper, </seg>
                    <seg corresp="#KR1e0008_tls_011-14a.12" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T08:37:34.618+09:00">with regard to its enhanced beauty, it was still acceptable.</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#KR1e0008_tls_012-4a.2" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T08:41:12.934+09:00">Field mice gnawed at the horns of the Jiao sacrificial bull.</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#KR1e0008_tls_012-4a.3" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T08:41:22.874+09:00">A bull was divined anew.</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#KR1e0008_tls_012-5a.2" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T08:41:36.59+09:00">Summer, fourth month, xinsi (day 18).</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#KR1e0008_tls_012-5a.3" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T08:42:51.821+09:00">Jiao sacrifice. Herewith the Chunqiu records of irregularities concerning the Jiao sacrifice are fully presented and explicated.</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#KR1e0008_tls_012-5a.4" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T08:43:05.89+09:00">For there is more to be said about the implications of these irregularities.</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#KR1e0008_tls_012-5a.5" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T08:43:15.912+09:00">“Field mice gnawed at the horns of the bull for the Jiao sacrifice.</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#KR1e0008_tls_012-5a.6" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T08:43:32.506+09:00">A bull was divined anew.”</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#KR1e0008_tls_012-5a.7" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T08:43:43.471+09:00">This was recorded to indicate irreverence,</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#KR1e0008_tls_012-5a.8" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T08:43:57.699+09:00">because it is when the curved horns of the Jiao sacrificial bull are examined daily to detect injuries</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#KR1e0008_tls_012-5a.9" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T08:44:12.959+09:00">that the proper principles of oversight are realized to their fullest indeed!</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#KR1e0008_tls_012-5a.10" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T08:44:24.893+09:00">The Jiao sacrifice is performed from the first to the third month.</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#KR1e0008_tls_012-5a.11" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T08:44:36.067+09:00">This is the proper season of the Jiao.</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#KR1e0008_tls_012-5a.12" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T08:44:47.184+09:00">To perform the Jiao in the fourth month of summer</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#KR1e0008_tls_012-5a.13" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T08:45:01.34+09:00">is untimely.</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#KR1e0008_tls_012-5a.14" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T08:45:12.865+09:00">To perform the Jiao in the fifth month of summer</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#KR1e0008_tls_012-5a.15" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T08:45:22.584+09:00">is untimely.</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#KR1e0008_tls_012-5a.16" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T08:45:32.217+09:00">The beginning of summer can be recognized as a continuation of the spring;</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#KR1e0008_tls_012-5a.17" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T08:45:46.299+09:00">but to recognize the end of autumn as the continuation of the beginning of spring</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#KR1e0008_tls_012-5a.18" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T08:45:56.066+09:00">is surely unacceptable.</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#KR1e0008_tls_012-5a.19" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T08:46:23.618+09:00">In the record “Ninth month the Jiao sacrifice was performed”,</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#KR1e0008_tls_012-5a.20" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T08:46:36.211+09:00">“performed”</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#KR1e0008_tls_012-5a.21" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T08:46:50.245+09:00">indicates it was not appropriate to perform.</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#KR1e0008_tls_012-5a.22" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T08:47:04.815+09:00">As for the Jiao sacrifice, three divinations</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#KR1e0008_tls_012-5a.23" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T08:47:12.058+09:00">accords with the rites;</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#KR1e0008_tls_012-5a.24" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T08:47:19.627+09:00">four divinations</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#KR1e0008_tls_012-5a.25" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T08:47:26.876+09:00">violates the rites;</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#KR1e0008_tls_012-5a.26" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T08:47:33.869+09:00">five divinations</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#KR1e0008_tls_012-5a.27" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T08:47:51.172+09:00">is far too extreme.</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#KR1e0008_tls_012-5a.28" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T08:48:03.459+09:00">When divining whether to release the sacrificial bull,</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#KR1e0008_tls_012-5a.29" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T08:48:13.289+09:00">if the divination is auspicious then the sacrificial bull is released;</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#KR1e0008_tls_012-5a.30" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T08:48:29.375+09:00">if not auspicious then the sacrificial bull is not released.</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#KR1e0008_tls_012-5a.31" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T08:48:53.528+09:00">When the bull is injured and the record does not mention the one who injured it,</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#KR1e0008_tls_012-5a.32" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T08:49:05.004+09:00">the injury was self-inflicted by the bull.</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#KR1e0008_tls_012-5a.33" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T08:49:16.88+09:00">For this reason the record uses wording indicating leniency.</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#KR1e0008_tls_012-5a.34" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T08:49:29.736+09:00">When unblemished it is called “a sacrificial bull”.</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#KR1e0008_tls_012-5a.35" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T08:50:41.459+09:00">When blemished</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#KR1e0008_tls_012-5a.37" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T08:50:03.366+09:00">In both cases, it is identified as “a bull”</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#KR1e0008_tls_012-5a.38" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T08:50:09.518+09:00">but the reason for considering it a bull in each case differs.</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#KR1e0008_tls_012-5a.36" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T08:51:01.636+09:00">or not yet prepared as a sacrificial bull, it is called “a bull”.</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#KR1e0008_tls_012-5a.39" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T08:51:12.793+09:00">When there are irregularities and the Jiao sacrifice is not performed,</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#KR1e0008_tls_012-5a.40" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T08:51:42.09+09:00">consequently it is divined whether to release the bull.</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#KR1e0008_tls_012-5a.41" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T08:51:53.143+09:00">If it is already considered a “bull”,</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#KR1e0008_tls_012-5a.42" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T08:52:04.509+09:00">why does one still divine whether to release it?</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#KR1e0008_tls_012-5a.43" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T08:52:16.795+09:00">According to the rites, it is preferable to preserve the bull rather than lose it.</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#KR1e0008_tls_012-5a.45" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T08:53:28.885+09:00">It had already been prepared for sacrifice to Shangdi.</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#KR1e0008_tls_012-5a.46" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T08:53:41.694+09:00">This is the reason why one must first divine before one releases it</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#KR1e0008_tls_012-5a.47" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T08:54:08.011+09:00">because one does not dare to act on one’s own authority.</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#KR1e0008_tls_012-5a.48" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T08:54:17.94+09:00">If the divination is inauspicious,</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#KR1e0008_tls_012-5a.49" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T08:54:28.789+09:00">what should be done?</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#KR1e0008_tls_012-5a.50" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T08:54:39.868+09:00">Do not release the bull</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#KR1e0008_tls_012-5a.51" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T08:54:49.174+09:00">but keep it in a secure place.</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#KR1e0008_tls_012-5a.52" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T08:55:08.217+09:00">Keep it tethered until the first jia day in the sixth month. Then on the first jia day begin to prepare it to become a sacrificial animal.</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#KR1e0008_tls_012-5a.53" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T08:55:23.787+09:00">Only then include it in your retinue of sacrificial animals.</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#KR1e0008_tls_012-5a.54" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T08:55:37.212+09:00">What the Master mentioned in his records</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#KR1e0008_tls_012-5a.55" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T08:55:44.979+09:00">concerns irregularities of the sacrificial bull.</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#KR1e0008_tls_012-5a.56" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T08:56:03.51+09:00">So what about the introductory claim: “In this one place, I will fully present and explicate the Chunqiu records of the irregularities concerning the Jiao sacrifice”?</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#KR1e0008_tls_012-5a.58" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T08:56:22.659+09:00">In the sixth month on the first jia day, we begin to prepare the sacrificial bull. </seg>
                    <seg corresp="#KR1e0008_tls_012-5a.59" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T08:56:33.517+09:00">In the tenth month on the first jia day, we begin to tether the sacrificial bull. </seg>
                    <seg corresp="#KR1e0008_tls_012-5a.60" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T08:56:49.97+09:00">In the eleventh</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#KR1e0008_tls_012-5a.61" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T08:57:03.179+09:00">and twelfth months, even if the sacrificial bull exhibits irregularities,</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#KR1e0008_tls_012-5a.62" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T08:57:12.617+09:00">we do not make a report.</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#KR1e0008_tls_012-5a.63" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T08:57:35.773+09:00">We wait until the first month of the new year and only after that month do we speak of irregularities of the sacrificial bull.</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#KR1e0008_tls_012-5a.64" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T08:57:47.404+09:00">This, then, is how to provide a full account of the Jiao sacrifice.</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#KR1e0008_tls_012-5a.65" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T08:57:57.591+09:00">The Jiao sacrifice exemplifies the proper way to make offerings.</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#KR1e0008_tls_012-5a.66" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T08:58:08.648+09:00">And so, when we honor its proper season</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#KR1e0008_tls_012-5a.67" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T08:58:17.763+09:00">and exalt its ritual rules</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#KR1e0008_tls_012-5a.68" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T08:58:32.818+09:00">then it is permissible to proceed even if in raising up the sacrificial bull minor imperfections occur.</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#KR1e0008_tls_012-5a.69" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T08:58:46.839+09:00">Why has the Master not made any record of divining for the Jiao sacrifice in the third month?</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#KR1e0008_tls_012-5a.71" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T08:58:59.518+09:00">“The Jiao sacrifice is performed from the first to the third month.</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#KR1e0008_tls_012-5a.72" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T08:59:19.508+09:00">This is the proper season for the Jiao.”</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#KR1e0008_tls_012-5a.73" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T08:59:39.04+09:00">And so in the twelfth month on the last xin day we divine for the first xin day of the first month. </seg>
                    <seg corresp="#KR1e0008_tls_012-5a.74" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T08:59:47.769+09:00">If the outcome is adverse,</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#KR1e0008_tls_012-5a.75" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T09:00:13.578+09:00">then we divine on the last xin day of the first month for the first xin day of the second month. </seg>
                    <seg corresp="#KR1e0008_tls_012-5a.76" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T09:00:23.92+09:00">If the outcome is adverse,</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#KR1e0008_tls_012-5a.77" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T09:00:31.603+09:00">then we divine on the last xin day of the second month for the first xin day of the third month. </seg>
                    <seg corresp="#KR1e0008_tls_012-5a.78" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T09:00:39.892+09:00">If the outcome is still adverse,</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#KR1e0008_tls_012-5a.79" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T09:06:06.961+09:00">then the Jiao sacrifice is not performed.</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#KR1e0008_tls_010-66a.2" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T09:06:48.531+09:00">Autumn.</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#KR1e0008_tls_010-66a.3" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T09:07:00.284+09:00">Inspection at Hong. </seg>
                    <seg corresp="#KR1e0008_tls_010-66a.4" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T09:07:09.835+09:00">It was proper.</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#KR1e0008_tls_010-66a.5" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T09:07:25.91+09:00">To avail oneself of the autumnal hunt to practice deploying military maneuvers</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#KR1e0008_tls_010-66a.6" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T09:07:38.091+09:00">was one of the great rituals.</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#KR1e0008_tls_010-66a.7" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T09:07:49.176+09:00">Cut down the undergrowth to create a protected space;</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#KR1e0008_tls_010-66a.8" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T09:08:07.282+09:00">Erect red standards to create a provisional entryway;</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#KR1e0008_tls_010-66a.9" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T09:08:16.146+09:00">Take coarse cloth and cover wooden blocks to create entryway posts,</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#KR1e0008_tls_010-66a.10" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T09:08:32.372+09:00">Those who proceed smoothly will do so with a fistful of space on either side;</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#KR1e0008_tls_010-66a.11" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T09:08:46.292+09:00">But the charioteers who ram the posts will not gain entry!</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#KR1e0008_tls_010-66a.12" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T09:08:59.428+09:00">Chariot upon chariot following tracks in the dust; </seg>
                    <seg corresp="#KR1e0008_tls_010-66a.13" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T09:09:12.208+09:00">Horse upon horse advancing hoof by hoof;</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#KR1e0008_tls_010-66a.14" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T09:09:20.675+09:00">Game in abundance to be caught;</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#KR1e0008_tls_010-66a.15" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T09:09:36.068+09:00">Only when the charioteers do not lose their proper pace</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#KR1e0008_tls_010-66a.16" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T09:09:46.914+09:00">can the archers hit their mark!</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#KR1e0008_tls_010-66a.17" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T09:10:06.372+09:00">Do not pursue those who go beyond the protected space (hunting/battle).</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#KR1e0008_tls_010-66a.18" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T09:10:23.696+09:00">Such is the principle that one does not pursue those who flee.</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#KR1e0008_tls_010-66a.19" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T09:10:37.907+09:00">Game with facial wounds must not be used for offerings,</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#KR1e0008_tls_010-66a.20" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T09:11:00.437+09:00">unwhole game must not be used for offerings. </seg>
                    <seg corresp="#KR1e0008_tls_010-66a.21" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T09:11:11.701+09:00">Even if game is caught in abundance,</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#KR1e0008_tls_010-66a.22" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T09:11:20.923+09:00">the Son of Heaven selects only thirty among them. </seg>
                    <seg corresp="#KR1e0008_tls_010-66a.23" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T09:11:34.237+09:00">The remaining game is distributed among the numerous rank and file officers for archery practice in the archery hall.</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#KR1e0008_tls_010-66a.24" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T09:11:47.643+09:00">Those who shoot and hit the mark,</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#KR1e0008_tls_010-66a.25" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T09:11:58.579+09:00">even if they did not acquire game during the hunt,</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#KR1e0008_tls_010-66a.26" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T09:12:08.752+09:00">will acquire game.</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#KR1e0008_tls_010-66a.27" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T09:12:21.542+09:00">Those who acquired game during the hunt but shoot and fail to hit the mark,</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#KR1e0008_tls_010-66a.28" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T09:12:32.8+09:00">will not acquire game.</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#KR1e0008_tls_010-66a.29" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T09:12:45.715+09:00">By this we know: that the ancients honored humaneness and righteousness</seg>
                    <seg corresp="#KR1e0008_tls_010-66a.30" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#jgentz" modified="2025-12-10T09:12:51.956+09:00">and scorned bravado and might.</seg>
                </p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
